{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "The Good Old Days", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Dreaming Big", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Adjectives About Feelings and Reactions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You talk about feelings and reactions using adjectives.  It is important to use the correct kind of adjective - it is common for English language learners to confuse the two kinds of adjectives when talking about feelings and reactions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "1. -ed adjectives", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed </span> are used to describe how a person <span class=\"strong\">feels</span>, like <span class=\"italic\">annoyed</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> fascinated</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> entertained</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> surprised</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> worried</span> or <span class=\"italic\"> tired</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I am annoyed. <br/> Parents are thrilled.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "2. -ing adjectives", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\">-ing </span> are used to describe things and situations, like <span class=\"italic\">annoying</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> entertaining</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> surprising</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> worrying</span> or <span class=\"italic\">tiring</span>. These adjectives describe the <span class=\"strong\">effect</span> something has on a person.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The study is compelling.</span> (It makes me feel compelled.)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Work is sometimes surprising, too.</span> (It makes me feel tired.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Media publicity ensured entertaining events. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Watching a celebrity play baseball became much more captivating than actually playing baseball.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Used to and Would", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would</span> and <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> have similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "However, there is an important difference between <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span>.<br><br>   <span class=\"strong\">Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> does not require this. <br><br>  Read the following example: <br>  <span class=\"italic\">We would visit India every summer when we were children.</span><br>  When we were children refers to a past time frame and therefore makes the meaning of would clear.<br><br>  <span class=\"italic\">We used to visit India every summer. </span><br>  Here, you do not have to include a past time frame since the meaning of <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> clear.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sports used to be largely amatuer events. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " As people began to watch more sporting events, they would play fewer sports themselves.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "sportsmanship", "type": "name"}, {"content": " fair play, following the rules of a game and being a good loser ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sports no longer focus on the lessons they used to teach, such as sportsmanship.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about sports and interests.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "couch potato ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a person who spends little or no time exercising and a lot of time watching television ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This trend, watching others play sports from the living room chair, created a phenomenon of being a \u201ccouch potato\".", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "amateur ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a non-professional", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: Sports used to be largely amateur events.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to capitalize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make money ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Promoters began to see the potential to capitalize on sports. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to exploit ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to use something or someone for personal gain", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A small number of athletes are exploited to provide entertainment for the masses.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "moral ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "honorable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: Games have become a source of profit and no longer focus on the lessons they used to teach - sportsmanship and moral development.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "With a partner, discuss this question: Do you think people care more about the game or the athlete? Why?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe your opinion using adjectives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Keep the discussion going by asking follow-up questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Try to come to a conclusion with your partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I discuss the issue of sports.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "My partner and I describe our opinion of sports.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I keep the discussion going by asking follow-up questions.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn7le08ob10re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn7le08ob10re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "Becoming a sports player nowadays is more than just being good at what you do. The dream is much bigger and much more complex than that. The situation in modern day sports is often compared to the 1920s - the decade that saw the rise of the celebrity sportsman. Many sports went through a period of transition in the 1920s."}, {"image": "engenn7le08ob10re2img02.jpg", "time": "18000", "id": 2, "text": "Sports used to be largely amateur events. Then, as promoters began to see the potential to capitalize on sports and bring in some money, changes began to happen. Professional football leagues, golf tours, and tennis circuits were organized. Media publicity ensured entertaining events that captivated audiences and guaranteed financial success. This meant raising salaries for the sports stars and allowing for the construction of new stadiums."}, {"image": "engenn7le08ob10re2img03.jpg", "time": "42500", "id": 3, "text": "As people began to watch more sporting events, they would play fewer sports themselves. This trend, which continues to the present day, created a phenomenon of being a \"couch potato\". Watching a celebrity play baseball became much more captivating than actually playing baseball. Money is such a factor in sports that sports have become commercialized to the point where now, a small number of athletes are exploited to provide entertainment for the masses. Games have become a source of profit and no longer focus on the lessons they used to teach - sportsmanship and moral development."}], "audiosrc": "engenn7le08ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le08ob10re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "  I can talk about sports and interests.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "  I can talk about feelings and reactions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about habits in the past. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "  Do you prefer to play sports or watch them on TV? Why? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How do you feel about the amount of money professional sports players earn?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Did you use to play sports when you were younger? What did you play?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "The celebrity sportsman ... is it about the game anymore?  ", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " \nSally's blog continues. This time she focuses on the sports industry <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">nowadays</span>.", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"},